lement-72ad9241 elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-featured-image elementor-widget-image" data-id="72ad9241" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-featured-image.default"> <div class="elementor-widget-container"> <img src="data:image/png;base64," title="Pte (19)" alt="Pte (19)" class="lzl" data-lzl-src="https://sumlingo.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pte-19-2.png"><noscript lzl=""><img src="https://sumlingo.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Pte-19-2.png" title="Pte (19)" alt="Pte (19)"></noscript> </div> </div> <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-453a88d9 elementor-align-left elementor-widget elementor-widget-post-info" data-id="453a88d9" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="post-info.default"> <div class="elementor-widget-container"> <ul class="elementor-inline-items elementor-icon-list-items elementor-post-info"> <li class="elementor-icon-list-item elementor-repeater-item-fde9fb9 elementor-inline-item" itemprop="datePublished"> <span class="elementor-icon-list-text elementor-post-info__item elementor-post-info__item--type-date">
										<time>June 2, 2025</time>					</span> </li> </ul> </div> </div> <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-2b2f0819 blog-content-part elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content" data-id="2b2f0819" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default"> <div class="elementor-widget-container"> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">If you are preparing for the Pearson Test of English (PTE) in 2025, one of the quickest and most scoring parts of the Speaking section is the <a href="https://sumlingo.com/blog/pte-answer-short-questions/">Answer Short Question task</a>. Although it seems simple, many candidates lose marks due to mishearing the question, hesitating, or giving incomplete answers. We provide a list of the most repeated 100 Answer Short Questions in the 2025 PTE exam based on recent feedback and exam updates. Practicing these can help boost your confidence and increase your speaking score.</p> <h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>What Is the Answer Short Question Task?</strong></h2> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">In this task, you will hear a question and must respond with a short, accurate answer, usually one or two words. The question may be factual, logical, or general knowledge-based. You do not need to use full sentences. For example:</p> <ul class="wp-block-list"> <li><strong>Question: </strong>What do we call a person who writes novels?</li> </ul> <p class="wp-block-paragraph" style="padding-right:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--50)"> <strong>Answer: </strong>Author</p> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">The key is to respond quickly and correctly.</p> <h2 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Why This Task Matters</strong></h2> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Though each Answer Short Question carries only a small portion of the total score, it contributes to both your Speaking and Listening marks. If you get several questions right, you can earn marks quickly.</p> <h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>Common challenges include:</strong></h3> <ul class="wp-block-list"> <li>Not understanding the accent</li> </ul> <ul class="wp-block-list"> <li>Speaking too softly or too late</li> </ul> <ul class="wp-block-list"> <li>Overthinking simple answers</li> </ul> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">That’s why practicing real, frequently repeated questions can make a big difference.</p> <h3 class="wp-block-heading"><strong>100 Most Repeated Answer Short Questions 2025</strong></h3> <p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is a curated list of the top 100 questions with their correct answers. These have been frequently reported by PTE candidates in recent tests.</p> <div class="wp-block-group is-style-default is-horizontal is-content-justification-left is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4f7a2c62 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex"> <p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>1.</strong> </p> <figure class="wp-block-audio"><audio controls src="https://sumlingo.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Audio1-2.mp3"></audio></figure> </div> <p class="wp-block-paragraph" style="padding-left:2rem"> <strong>Question</strong>: What do we call a doctor who performs operations?</p> <p class="wp-block-paragraph" style="padding-left:2rem"> <strong>Answer</strong>: Surgeon</p> <div class="wp-block-group is-style-default is-horizontal is-content-justification-left is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-4f7a2c62 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex"> <p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>2.</strong> </p> <figure class="wp-block-audio"><audio controls src="https://sumlingo.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Audio2-2.mp3"></audio></figure> </div> <p class="wp-block-paragraph" style="padding-left:2rem"> <strong>Question</strong>: What is the device used to take photographs?</p> <p class="wp-block-paragraph" style="padding-left:2rem"> <strong>Answer</strong>: Camera</p> <div class="wp-block-group is-style-default is-horizontal is-content-justification-left is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-contain